// Chain-block (2026-08-19, new): after pass 2 of a chain, an escalating
// chance per extra pass tries to force-redraw column 1/2/3 into a
// non-connecting position (reusing the same RGS-safe redraw as the
// force-deadspin mechanism below). If every column fails to find a valid
// position, the block defers and retries on the NEXT pass until it lands.
// Locked params from real_chain_damping_sweep.py / chain_block_pending_mechanism.py.
const CHAIN_BLOCK_THRESHOLD = 2;
const CHAIN_BLOCK_STEP = 0.30;
// Hard cap (2026-08-19, new): the probabilistic chain-block above already
// escalates to a 100% attempt rate by pass 5, but the deferred-retry can -
// vanishingly rarely - keep failing for many passes in a row if the board
// keeps landing in a genuinely locked state (every candidate on every
// column would still connect). That produced an observed max chain of 29
// passes. This hard cap forces the block through unconditionally at pass
// 16 via a relaxed redraw (see routeColumnForceDeadspinRelaxed) that only
// avoids an EXACT name match with the immediate neighbor - it does not
// honor the "any wild nearby blocks everything" rule the normal mechanism
// does, so it carries a small residual connect-risk, but it always
// succeeds, guaranteeing max chain length stays at or under this value.
const HARD_CHAIN_CAP = 16;
// One-shot debug override (UI-only): set by the "Force next chain to hit
// hard cap" test button to a small value so the hard cap is easy to
// trigger/observe live; consumed (reset to null) the instant it fires.
// Stays null forever in the headless self-check / Node-extracted sim,
